# LF FOR EVERY SHELL SCRIPT, DECIDED ONCE INSTEAD OF REMEMBERED.
#
# A CRLF shebang fails on the server with «No such file or directory» — about bash itself, which
# is the most misleading error in this pipeline: it names the interpreter when the fault is an
# invisible byte at the end of line one. The deploy guard has caught it FOUR times, twice because
# an edit from a Windows editor re-introduced it minutes after it was fixed.
#
# A rule in the repository ends that loop. The guard stays, because it also catches files this
# pattern does not cover.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
